        updated_by: "po/decision-consumption-20260721T1811",
        po_closure_20260721T1811: "CLOSED — ACCEPTANCE MET, NOT ABANDONED, AND NOT DISPATCHED. This spike's acceptance was 'findings doc names WHICH of (a)/(b)/(c) is live, with live evidence (not inference)'. That is satisfied: cowork-team — the accused actor — answered it in signal cowork-team-20260721T172415Z (committed e015c2c43 at 17:25:44Z, i.e. AFTER I formed the batch, which is why the row was minted at all). ANSWER: (a) flow non-compliance — the WORK-continuation drain body is narrated but not executed. Router verified the answer at source rather than accepting the accused's self-report, which is the part that lets me close this: scripts/agents-flow/drain-signals.js:6 declares READ-marking explicitly OUT of script scope and left to the flow, and the flow half was never run. (b) is excluded because no write was ever attempted; (c) is excluded because the 17:00Z and 17:15Z ticks had ZERO slots. Prior-art memory feedback_cowork_spawn_narrates_not_executes predicted exactly this shape and was the cheapest candidate — it was right. Dispatching a diagnosis spike to re-derive a settled answer would be pure churn. NO NEW ROW MINTED for the fix: router verified two existing BACKLOG rows already own it — FIX-COWORK-STEP0A-TOPO-DRAIN-STATUS-CONTRACT (PLAN-ONLY, next_agent=ba) and FIX-SIGNALQUEUE-RECEIVER-DELIVERY-CONTRACT (PLAN-ONLY, owner=po, next_agent=architect) — and cowork-team itself requested fold-in rather than a new row. Remediation folds into FIX-COWORK-STEP0A-TOPO-DRAIN-STATUS-CONTRACT, which now carries the blocking ordering constraint and the live-probe protection (see its po_fold_from_spike_20260721T1811).",
        po_closure_carries_forward_20260721T1811: "TWO THINGS MUST SURVIVE THIS CLOSURE — both transcribed onto the fold target so closing this row does not drop them. (1) THE ORDERING CONSTRAINT IS BLOCKING AND COUNTERINTUITIVE: fixing cowork compliance FIRST converts a dormant defect into ACTIVE DATA LOSS. dev-team/flow/drain-signals.md:22 collects only status==NEW rows and :69 makes READ rows the prunable class, so if cowork Step 0a starts marking to:po rows READ as written, every cowork->dev-team escalation becomes invisible to dev-team's own drain and evicts within 24h. cowork's non-compliance has been ACCIDENTALLY PROTECTIVE. Settle the status contract BEFORE enforcing compliance. (2) THE LIVE PROBE STAYS: signal row po-20260720T052606 remains deliberately at NEW as the only reproducing instance. Do NOT mark it READ as tidy-up; mark it READ only as the verified OUTPUT of a confirmed fix. Also carried: the second-order cost is real and ongoing — with >=1 NEW cowork-addressed row the SILENT gate can never fire, so every cowork tick burns a full LLM read every 15 minutes; the defect sustains the exact condition that defeats the optimisation. That is the cost clock running on the fold target."
      } )
  ]
| .task_board.ready = [ .task_board.ready[] | select(.id != "SPIKE-COWORK-DRAIN-BODY-NOT-EXECUTING-ON-WORK-TICKS") ]

# ─── 5b. FOLD TARGET — carry the constraints + endorse the prune deferral ─────
| upd("backlog"; "FIX-COWORK-STEP0A-TOPO-DRAIN-STATUS-CONTRACT"; {
  po_fold_from_spike_20260721T1811: "FOLD-IN from SPIKE-COWORK-DRAIN-BODY-NOT-EXECUTING-ON-WORK-TICKS (closed 2026-07-21T18:11Z, acceptance met). THE DIAGNOSIS IS SETTLED — do not re-run it: the live failure mode is (a) flow non-compliance, the WORK-continuation drain body is narrated but not executed. Verified at source by router, not accepted from the accused actor's self-report: scripts/agents-flow/drain-signals.js:6 declares READ-marking explicitly OUT of script scope and left to the flow; the flow half never ran. (b) excluded — no write was ever attempted. (c) excluded — the 17:00Z and 17:15Z ticks had ZERO slots. Prior art: feedback_cowork_spawn_narrates_not_executes. BLOCKING ORDERING CONSTRAINT, and it inverts the obvious remedy: do NOT fix cowork compliance first. dev-team/flow/drain-signals.md:22 collects only status==NEW rows and :69 makes READ rows the prunable class — so the moment cowork Step 0a starts marking to:po rows READ as written, every cowork->dev-team escalation becomes invisible to dev-team's own drain and cold-evicts within 24h. cowork's non-compliance has been ACCIDENTALLY PROTECTIVE of that bridge. THIS ROW's status contract must be settled BEFORE compliance is enforced anywhere — that ordering is the whole reason this row, not a fresh fix row, is the fold target. LIVE PROBE — DO NOT TIDY: signal row po-20260720T052606 is deliberately held at NEW as the only reproducing instance; mark it READ only as the verified OUTPUT of a confirmed fix. COST CLOCK: with >=1 NEW cowork-addressed row the preflight SILENT gate can never fire, so every cowork tick burns a full LLM read every 15 min (the script header states SILENT was meant to cover ~80% of ticks). The defect sustains the condition that defeats the optimisation — this is not a static backlog item. Sibling row FIX-SIGNALQUEUE-RECEIVER-DELIVERY-CONTRACT (owner=po, next_agent=architect) covers the adjacent delivery-contract half; keep them coherent, they share the status-semantics question.",

  po_ruling_signalqueue_prune_deferral_20260721T1811: "ROUTER'S 0a-D PRUNE DEFERRAL IS ENDORSED — AND IT SHOULD STOP BEING RE-LITIGATED EVERY TICK, WHICH IS WHY IT IS RECORDED HERE ON THE OWNING ROW RATHER THAN LEFT AS A PER-TICK JUDGEMENT CALL. Router has now deferred the 0a-D signal_queue prune for THREE consecutive dev-team ticks. That is correct and I am ratifying it, not merely tolerating it: the prune removes READ/RESOLVED rows, drain-signals.md:69 makes READ rows the prunable class, and THIS ROW is open on precisely whether that severs the cowork->dev-team escalation bridge. Running the prune now would destroy the evidence cowork-team warned about and would resolve the open question by deleting its subject. STANDING INSTRUCTION: 0a-D stays deferred until this row's status contract is settled. A deferral driven by a documented open question is not a skipped chore and must not be counted as drift or auto-escalated as a stalled step. When this row closes, the prune is unblocked automatically — no separate PO ruling needed to re-enable it. Nobody needs to ask again in the meantime."
})

# ─── 2. MINT ONE ROW (the only mint this cycle) ───────────────────────────────
| .task_board.backlog += [ {
  id: "FIX-BCTC-NEWSCHAIN-FALLBACK-ZEROS-WRITE-TARGET",
  type: "FIX",
  title: "news-chain BCTC fallback writes an all-zeros balance sheet into financial_reports — the authoritative table — where it is byte-indistinguishable from OCR corruption at serve time; decide whether it should write there AT ALL before guarding arm (b2)",
  status: "BACKLOG",
  priority: "HIGH",
  size: "M",
  zone: "apps/mcp-server",
  owner: "po",
  next_agent: "ba",
  plan_only: true,
  supervised: true,
  depends: [],
  created_at: $ts,
  created_by: "po/decision-consumption-20260721T1811",
  updated_at: $ts,
  updated_by: "po/decision-consumption-20260721T1811",
  parent_finding: "FIX-BCTC-REPARSE-BATCH-CORRUPTION-NGAYNOP-FLIP (QA round-2 approval, router_confirmed_sibling_gap_is_arm_b2_only)",

  origin: "QA found this sibling writer while approving arm (b2) on parseBctcReport.ts::storeReport(), and explicitly DECLINED to mint or to expand that row (correctly — PO had a scope-hold on it). Router sharpened the finding at source and also declined to mint. Minting is PO's; this is that mint.",

  mechanism: "newsChainFallback.ts (apps/mcp-server/src/application/usecases/bctc/newsChainFallback.ts) is a SECOND, independently-implemented writer to the same financial_reports (action_code, sort_key) row as storeReport(). It already has arm (b1): lines 264-274 block the write when existingReportRow.total_assets > 0, preserving a previously-good row and logging BLOCKED. What it LACKS is arm (b2): with NO prior row it proceeds to INSERT a brand-new row whose totalAssets is a hardcoded 0 (line 307, bound into the INSERT at line 535), inside an entire all-zeros balance sheet at lines 304-313. Identical defect shape to the one just fixed in storeReport(): refuses to overwrite a good row, but freely CREATES a fresh zero-total row that bctcIdentityGuard.ts then reads at serve time as the OCR-corruption fingerprint. The file's own comment at lines 254-263 already says it 'carried the same two defects' and 'mirrors the identical guard' — the mirror was completed for only one of the two arms.",

  po_verified_at_source_20260721T1811: "PO RE-READ THE FILE THIS TICK rather than accepting QA's or router's description, and the single decisive fact checks out: `totalAssets: 0` at line 307 is a hardcoded LITERAL and is the ONLY assignment to that field in the whole file (grep: refs at 73, 255, 307, 425, 535 — 307 is the sole write, 535 binds it to the INSERT, 425 is the SQL column list, 255 is the comment, 73 is the summary formatter). There is NO code path in this function that can produce a non-zero balance sheet. The surrounding lines 304-313 are likewise all-zero literals across currentAssets, nonCurrentAssets, liabilities, equity and totalLiabilitiesAndEquity.",

  product_question_decide_before_scoping: "ANSWER THIS FIRST — the fix does not follow from the defect. Question as router framed it: if a news-inference fallback only ever produces directional hints and never real balance-sheet figures, is writing it into financial_reports — the table bctcIdentityGuard treats as authoritative at serve time — the actual design error, such that guarding arm (b2) alone merely relocates the problem? PO'S STRONG STEER, WITH THE PROOF: YES, IT IS THE DESIGN ERROR, and here is the reductio that settles it. Arm (b1) already blocks every write where a good row exists. Arm (b2), applied literally, blocks every write where NO row exists AND totalAssets<=0. Since totalAssets is hardcoded 0 on EVERY call (verified above — no path produces otherwise), the two arms together block 100% of this function's writes. Adding arm (b2) does not fix the function; it silently converts it into a total no-op while leaving ~600 lines of live, tested, maintained code in place pretending to be a working fallback. A guard that makes its own subject unreachable is not a guard — it is proof that the write target is wrong. CORROBORATING, AND THE PART THAT MAKES THIS USER-FACING RATHER THAN MERELY UNTIDY: (i) the code's OWN comment at lines 254-259 already concedes the whole argument — 'this fallback ALWAYS writes totalAssets=0 ... it reconstructs directional hints from news signals, never real balance-sheet figures — i.e. every call is, by construction, the exact OCR-corruption fingerprint bctcIdentityGuard.ts checks for at serve time.' The codebase has already diagnosed itself; nobody drew the conclusion. (ii) The write is strictly WORSE than not writing, because it destroys an honest signal: an absent row serves 'Chua co du lieu BCTC' ('we do not have this'), whereas a zeros row serves '[CORRUPT DATA - SKIP] total_assets=0 (OCR extraction failure)' — a false claim that we HAVE the filing and it is broken, which misattributes a defect to the filer. This is the same family of harm as the ngay_nop flip on the parent row: fabricating a state that defames a real-world filing. (iii) buildAnalysisSummary() at line 73 formats this into Vietnamese RAG-retrievable prose — 'Tong tai san: 0 trieu dong.' — a flat factual assertion that the company has zero total assets, written into the retrieval corpus. That is fabricated financial data in a served surface, and it engages feedback_no_fake_data_real_fetch directly. THEREFORE the design target to evaluate is: directional news-inference hints belong in a hints/signals surface, NOT in financial_reports. BA must still evaluate the alternatives honestly (a separate table/column; a nullable-financials sentinel row explicitly marked non-authoritative that bctcIdentityGuard excludes; or deleting the write path entirely and keeping the function as a pure read-side hint producer) — my steer is not a pre-selected implementation, and if BA finds a consumer that genuinely needs these rows in financial_reports, say so and I will revisit.",

  six_tests_encode_the_defect: "THE HARD PART, AND WHY THIS IS A PO/BA ROW AND NOT A FIXER TICKET. SIX existing tests assert the first-ever zero-total write SUCCEEDING, i.e. they encode the defect as intended behaviour: 1294b-bctc-fallback RED-1 / RED-6 / RED-7 / RED-8-first-call (VCB/VIC/BSR/VJC first-call, all no-prior-row first-ever writes asserting fallback:true + row-exists), and BOTH cases in FIX-BCTC-NEWS-CHAIN-FALLBACK-ID-ORPHAN (run#1 explicitly commented first-ever-write, asserting fallback:true + row-exists for Q1 and Q2 sort_keys). QA adjudicated these individually and confirmed they are genuine intent-assertions, not incidental fixture inconvenience — that adjudication is accepted and must NOT be re-derived. These six are IN SCOPE to be rewritten by this row, and rewriting them is the deliverable that encodes whatever product answer is chosen. They are also the reason a quiet patch is impossible: any honest fix turns six green tests red, and a developer without this row's authority would reasonably read that as 'my change is wrong' and revert — which is EXACTLY what happened once already (see prior_attempt_reverted).",

  prior_attempt_reverted: "dev-mcp-server ALREADY TRIED the naive fix during the parent row's arm-(b2) work: applied the storeReport guard pattern to tryNewsChainFallback(), broke those 6 tests, and reverted cleanly — documenting it as an open gap in usecases.md rather than folding it in. That was the RIGHT call under a scope-hold and is not a failure; it is corroboration that the naive patch is blocked by design intent, not by a fixable test bug. Do not re-attempt the naive guard.",

  containment_do_not_downgrade: "BLAST RADIUS IS BOUNDED — THIS IS LATENT, NOT BLEEDING, WHICH IS WHY IT IS HIGH AND NOT P0. Router grep-confirmed the containment independently of QA: enableBctcFallback is declared optional at bctc/types.ts:59, DEFAULTS TO false at fetchParseAndStoreBctc.ts:50 (destructured `enableBctcFallback = false`), and resolvePdfText.ts:228 gates the fallback call behind `if (!enableBctcFallback)`. No non-test caller passes it true. THE FLAG IS THE CONTAINMENT AND MUST BE RECORDED AS SUCH — two failure modes to pre-empt: (1) nobody may downgrade this row on the grounds that 'the flag is false so it is safe' — the flag being false is WHY this is HIGH rather than P0, it is already priced in, and re-applying it is double-counting; (2) NOBODY MAY ENABLE enableBctcFallback ANYWHERE — test, staging or production — UNTIL THIS ROW IS CLOSED. Flipping that flag with arm (b2) open turns a latent hole into live manufacture of corrupt authoritative financial rows, on the exact mechanism the parent row was minted to stop. If a future task needs the fallback enabled, it depends on this row.",

  acceptance: "(1) A written product decision on where news-chain fallback output belongs, stated on this row before any code is scoped — either 'not in financial_reports' (PO's steer) with the replacement surface named, or a reasoned rebuttal naming the consumer that requires those rows in financial_reports. (2) The chosen design implemented such that no all-zeros row is ever CREATED in financial_reports by this path. (3) The six tests named in six_tests_encode_the_defect rewritten to assert the CHOSEN behaviour, with each rewrite's intent stated — not deleted, not skipped, not left asserting the old contract. (4) get_bctc_full for a ticker with no real filing serves honest absence ('Chua co du lieu BCTC'), never '[CORRUPT DATA - SKIP] total_assets=0' manufactured by this path. (5) Arm (b1) behaviour is preserved unchanged — a previously-good stored report is still never overwritten. (6) If the write path is removed entirely, buildAnalysisSummary()'s zero-valued Vietnamese output (line 73) must not reach any served or RAG-retrievable surface either — check that plane explicitly, do not assume removing the INSERT covers it.",

  verification_gate: "MECHANISM-SCOPED AND FULLY CODE-LEVEL — deliberately carries NO ingest, deploy-window or multi-day dependency, unlike the parent row (this is why it can converge in one pass). (a) A forced/simulated news-chain fallback invocation for a ticker with NO prior financial_reports row creates NO row — asserted against the live serving path via get_bctc_full returning 'Chua co du lieu BCTC', not by reading the DB plane directly (parent-row precedent: the DB plane and the serving plane diverged and only the serving plane matters here). (b) Same invocation for a ticker WITH a good stored row leaves it untouched and still serving non-zero total_assets (arm b1 regression). (c) grep proves no remaining code path can bind a hardcoded zero balance sheet into a financial_reports INSERT. (d) RED-before demonstrated by git-stash A/B with the test changes kept, same technique dev-mcp-server used on the parent row's arm (b2). (e) Full suite run and every failure file-attributed, not name-grepped — 1405b-bctc-vps-fixes.test.ts is a known decoy (has 'bctc' in the filename, its failures are in the unrelated logVpsPush group and are a test-order flake).",

  scope_boundaries: "DOES NOT own re-extraction or remediation of any already-corrupt or absent report — that stays with OPS-BCTC-REFINE-REPASS-NONBANK-5T, W5-FU-CTG-REFINE-96e36139 and SPIKE-BCTC-Q1-2026-SERVABILITY-CENSUS. DOES NOT own the parent row's storeReport() arm (b2), which is shipped and QA-approved. DOES NOT own the ingest-stall cohort (FIX-BCTC-Q1-2026-STORED-PDF-INGEST-STALL-15T) — per the parent row's po_acceptance_reconciliation, 13/16 of that cohort predate the reparse by four days and are NOT this mechanism. DOES NOT own the scale-signature corruption class (FIX-BCTC-VALIDATION-GATE-NONBANK-ZERO-SCALE, e.g. BSR total_assets=166.52 vs equity=145892845365) — different fingerprint, different row.",

  why_ba_first: "plan_only + next_agent=ba because acceptance (1) is a design decision with a real alternatives space (separate surface vs non-authoritative sentinel row vs delete the write path), and the six-test rewrite in (3) must encode whichever answer wins. Sending this straight to a developer would force a fixer to make a product call mid-patch — the precise trap that produced the earlier revert.",

  refs: [
    "feedback_no_fake_data_real_fetch",
    "feedback_nonzero_values_need_plausibility_check",
    "feedback_empty_read_is_not_evidence_confirm_tool_targets_store",
    "feedback_composite_score_masks_dead_detector_pruned_table",
    "project_data_serve_integrity"
  ]
} ]

